  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Disaster Risk Reduction project in Morne L&apos;Hopital</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">After the earthquake, Caritas Port-au-Prince has been involved in a disaster risk reduction project in Morne l&#x2019;Hopital, the mountain that surrounds Port-au-Prince. This project presented to CAFOD will contribute to improve the environmental conditions of the population of Saint Jude Parish by reducing the potential risk of flooding and mudslides in Morne l&#x2019;Hopital and by stabilizing and rehabilitating the ravines that endanger the communities living in the settlements below. 
This project is of particular importance, not just for the environmental rehabilitation/disaster mitigation and their infusion of much needed cash into destitute communities affected by the earthquake, but also because they represent a shift from relief to recovery and reconstruction &#x2013; offering long term benefits for the targeted communities.
With the expertise of Caritas Port-au-Prince, the communities living in the areas will build labor-intensive rock walls throughout the course of the ravines, which will serve to break flood waters and trap topsoil runoff, protecting the watershed, preventing mudslides and decreasing flooding in Port au Prince.
At the same time 10 community organizations will be supported by Caritas Port-au-Prince through training on soil conservation, tree nursery, reforestation and technical skills to make the system sustainable.</narrative>
  </description>
